# [6MAN](../wg/6man.html)

## Summary

The 6MAN working group met at IETF 127. The session covered administration updates, active working group draft presentations, and individual document proposals. 

Key leadership updates were announced: Jen Linkova stepped down as co-chair to serve as Internet Area Director, and Eric Kline joined Bob Hinden as 6MAN co-chair alongside Éric Vyncke as Area Director. 

The working group reviewed document status, open errata, and polled the room regarding resuming work on `draft-ietf-6man-rfc4291bis`. Further discussions covered IEEE 802.11 multicast reliability (`draft-ietf-6man-ieee80211-dms`), expanding the IPv6 loopback prefix (`draft-ietf-6man-loopback`), extension header enforcement at destination nodes (`draft-ietf-6man-eh-occurrences`), hierarchical CGA (`draft-buraglio-6man-hcga`), RoCEv2 load balancing using the flow label (`draft-cheng-6man-rocev2-flow-label`), ICMP error handling in SRv6 VPNs (`draft-alivar-spring-icmp-error-srv6-vpn`), and the AERO/OMNI adaptation layer specs.

