### IPv6 Issues with 802.11 Multicast Reliability (DMS)
- **Presentation:** [IPv6 issues with 802.11 multicast reliability remain (DMS)](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-6man-ipv6-issues-with-80211-multicast-reliability-remain-dms-00) presented by David Lamparter.
- **Draft:** `draft-ietf-6man-ieee80211-dms`
- **Technical Content:** The draft was restructured to emphasize Directed Multicast Service (DMS) over Flexible Multicast Service (FMS). It documents multicast drops caused by client power-save sleep states, missing MLD state sync during layer 2 AP roaming, and dropping of solicited-node multicast messages. It also incorporates unicast RA mechanisms.
- **Discussion:**
  - Ted Lemon highlighted roaming and mDNS issues, suggesting coordination with the Matter ecosystem.
  - Lucien Avramov discussed AP behaviors during roaming and advocated for host-initiated Router Solicitations (RS) over AP-side RA buffering.
  - Smith Kennedy supported multi-prong approaches, noting enterprise vendor support for layer 2 unicast conversion.
  - Éric Vyncke noted that the document is tracked in regular IEEE 802.11 / IETF coordination meetings.
  - Suresh Krishnan advised structuring Section 6 as a focused liaison statement to the Wi-Fi Alliance/IEEE with explicit recommendations.
  - Lorenzo Colitti suggested distinguishing host vs. AP behaviors clearly and evaluating whether hosts should re-subscribe to MLD groups upon roaming.

