### Enforcement of IPv6 Extension Headers Ordering and Occurrence at Destination Nodes
- **Presentation:** [Enforcement of IPv6 Extension Headers Ordering and Occurrence at Destination Nodes](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-6man-enforcement-of-ipv6-extension-headers-ordering-and-occurrence-at-destination-nodes-00) presented by Justin Iurman.
- **Draft:** `draft-ietf-6man-eh-occurrences`
- **Technical Content:** Updates RFC 8200 to allow destination nodes to enforce ordering and occurrence rules (Section 4.1) for extension headers to protect against parser exploits. Non-compliant packets MAY be dropped and trigger an ICMPv6 Parameter Problem message. Sender behavior requirements remain unchanged (recommended).
- **Discussion:**
  - Brian Carpenter raised his list proposal to make header ordering a normative MUST for senders.
  - Tim Wicinski / room comment noted that test programs like USGv6 and IPv6 Ready already treat EH ordering as mandatory for senders.
  - The authors plan to keep sender behavior as a recommendation unless explicit WG consensus indicates otherwise.

