### ICMP Error Handling for VPNs in SRv6 Networks
- **Presentation:** [ICMP Error Handling for VPNs in SRv6 Networks](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-6man-icmp-error-handling-for-vpns-in-srv6-networks-00) presented by Ferenc Fejes.
- **Draft:** `draft-alivar-spring-icmp-error-srv6-vpn`
- **Technical Content:** Outlines three methods to propagate ICMP errors back to SRv6 VPN Customer Edge (CE) nodes when intermediate Provider (P) nodes generate errors:
  1. P node tunnels ICMP errors directly to the egress PE.
  2. Ingress PE sets the tunnel source IP to a VPN-specific SID.
  3. Ingress PE loops back errors via its loopback to the egress PE to resolve the VPN context.
- **Discussion:**
  - Martin Horneffer asked if Method 2 handles overlapping IP space across different VPNs.
  - Joel Halpern clarified that binding the tunnel source address to the ingress PE's VPN SID fully disambiguates the VPN context.
  - Jie Dong suggested consolidating the three proposed mechanisms to reduce protocol options.
  - Eric Kline reminded participants that official document adoption and technical progression are taking place in the SPRING WG.

