### Automatic Extended Route Optimization and the Overlay Multilink Network Interface (AERO/OMNI)
- **Presentation:** [Automatic Extended Route Optimization and the Overlay Multilink Network Interface (AERO/OMNI)](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-6man-automatic-extended-route-optimization-and-the-overlay-multilink-network-interface-aeroomni-00) presented by Fred Templin.
- **Drafts:** `draft-templin-aero`, `draft-templin-omni`
- **Technical Content:** Proposes an adaptation layer between Layer 2 and Layer 3 to establish non-broadcast mobile access virtual overlay links, enabling mobile multi-homing and provider-independent addressing for end user devices.
- **Poll:** "have you read one or more of this document set?"
  - **Results:** yes: 3, no: 13, no_opinion: 0 (total: 67)
- **Discussion:**
  - Jen Linkova requested a clearer problem statement and explicit operator use cases.
  - Nick Buraglio and Joel Jaeggli compared the proposal to existing overlay technologies (e.g., WireGuard, LISP), noting that deployment friction has historically limited user adoption of complex host overlay mechanisms.
  - Joel Jaeggli did not support adopting the document set.

